[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ManualPage" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/components/manual_page.gd" id="1_page"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
title = "THERMAL"
body = "The module loses heat to the exterior, which runs near -60 C. The heater runs on LIFE SUPPORT and holds the cabin near 21 C.

If the heater loses power the cabin cools fast. Below 10 C you lose dexterity. Below 3 C exposure becomes dangerous. Pipes freeze near 1 C.

If you return to a cold module: restore life support first, then watch the temperature trend. The heater is not fast.

HEATER FAULT. Carry the multimeter to the engine-bay THERMAL probe and press E; check STATUS for HEATER MAIN. Sensor drift as well as an open heater needs service. In SHIP CONTROL / POWER turn LIFE SUPPORT OFF. Carry the wrench to THERMAL: OPEN HEATER MAIN COVER, REFIT HEATER MAIN (one gasket from stores; service time passes), CLOSE HEATER MAIN COVER. Restore LIFE SUPPORT and verify the fault cleared and cabin temperature recovers. See DIAGNOSTICS. Keep the essential-service outage short."
